rota lap 4143, row 3 -- Water, Venus, care and flow, the row that tastes. Threshold foundations/20260826-021734_water-the-row-that-tastes.md, then The Shape You Grew and the Shape You Are, The Happy Zone and the Thin Edge, and Growing a Language. What it surfaced: the cardinal seat's first question -- what smaller thing already works, and can this grow from it -- is not only a lens on a design, it is a policy a machine can run. Turning Gall's law into an allocator is this lap's whole finding, and the row asked the question that produced it.
file tools/fixtures/t/topology_growth_scan.sh the instrument -- five allocation policies at six occupancies over four Cayley graphs, with a leg word so a control can break one reading cheaply
file tools/fixtures/t/topology_growth_control.sh eleven plants through the shared plant.sh helper, nine breaking a named reading and two passing on purpose under a leg that cannot read them
file tools/t/topology_growth_witness.rish binds every figure by name, the theorem at the value its argument gives rather than the value the scan printed, and the mirror on all three coordinate shapes
file external-research/20260907-045627_what-an-address-space-costs-while-it-is-still-filling.md the paper, Gauge Field, graded B+ 88, proposed with no design claim in the checkable room
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri seats topology_growth at tier cadence, with the why written where a reader meets the guard
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260907.md the misordered pair swapped, which closes the index_row_bound red on metal
recommend check in (Keaton) -- four want your word, and the first is an apology with a mechanism attached. I DAMAGED TWO PEERS' WORK (red 20260907.051030, by stamp): stopping my own hot pass I ran pkill -f standing_equipment_run and then a ps|grep|kill loop, and BOTH MATCH A PROGRAM NAME while eight ships run that program from eight trees on one pier -- two peer hot passes died mid-flight and Pheromone's monitor restarted its loop. I found it by reading ps again and seeing cwd=grain-petrichor on the process I had just called mine. %291 guards a file moving; a signal is not a file, so no rule reached it. Habit repaired and proven on this lap -- filter every candidate by readlink -f /proc/<pid>/cwd and print the spared by tree. THE ASK: a tools/f/ helper every seat calls rather than kill, refusing any PID outside the caller's root, which makes the safe form the easy one; six ships run such a file, so it inherits %515's reason to go slowly. SECOND, THE ROOT I NAMED AND DID NOT TAKE: the shelf misorder has fired eleven times across four laps and is hand-repaired each time, and fold_shelf_link already ruled the identical sentence one room over -- may I tool the shelf sort? My own hand-fold lost a link depth on this very lap, which is the ask answering itself. THIRD, A RED I LEFT OPEN ON PURPOSE: fleet_watch reds under the roster and passes both alone and under ten CPU-bound processes; I found a bare sleep 1 where every neighbouring leg polls, and I did NOT repair it, because a root I cannot make fire is a guess and a fix closes on metal. Repair on a candidate root, or leave it reported? FOURTH, THE PAPER'S BUILDABLE for BAKERY: publish the address space in breadth-first order -- one array computed once, the allocator stays a bare counter, measured at 1.1% premium against 24x payout. That one is a decision about Comlink's address space rather than a measurement, and I have only priced four candidates against each other.
